### Example 3: Month-End Claims Submission Burst Handling

**Context**: Provider claims submission deadlines (last day of month) generate 4-8x normal traffic. Without burst allowance, token bucket would reject 60-70% of requests.

**Implementation** (ASP.NET Core Token Bucket):

```csharp
public class TokenBucketRateLimiter
{
    private readonly IDistributedCache _cache;

    public async Task<RateLimitResult> CheckLimitAsync(
        string consumerId,
        int refillRate,  // Tokens per minute
        int bucketCapacity)  // Max tokens (includes burst)
    {
        var key = $"rate_limit:token_bucket:{consumerId}";
        var bucketJson = await _cache.GetStringAsync(key);

        TokenBucket bucket = string.IsNullOrEmpty(bucketJson)
            ? new TokenBucket { Tokens = bucketCapacity, LastRefillTime = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeSeconds() }
            : JsonSerializer.Deserialize<TokenBucket>(bucketJson);

        // Calculate token refill
        var currentTime = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeSeconds();
        var timeElapsed = currentTime - bucket.LastRefillTime;
        var tokensToAdd = timeElapsed * (refillRate / 60.0);  // Convert to tokens/sec

        bucket.Tokens = Math.Min(bucket.Tokens + tokensToAdd, bucketCapacity);
        bucket.LastRefillTime = currentTime;

        if (bucket.Tokens >= 1)
        {
            bucket.Tokens -= 1;
            await _cache.SetStringAsync(key, JsonSerializer.Serialize(bucket),
                new DistributedCacheEntryOptions { AbsoluteExpirationRelativeToNow = TimeSpan.FromHours(1) });

            return new RateLimitResult { Allowed = true, RemainingTokens = (int)bucket.Tokens };
        }

        return new RateLimitResult { Allowed = false, RetryAfter = 60 };
    }
}

// Configuration: 1000 req/min base, 1500 capacity (50% burst)
var result = await rateLimiter.CheckLimitAsync(providerId, 1000, 1500);
```

**Outcomes**:
- **Burst Absorption**: Month-end traffic spikes (4-8x) handled without rejections during initial burst window
- **User Experience**: Claims submission time maintained at normal levels during burst absorption period
- **Cost Efficiency**: Burst allowance absorbed traffic spikes without triggering unnecessary auto-scaling

