#### Event Loop Lag Detection and Health Check Degradation

The Node.js event loop is single-threaded. When event loop lag is high, the service is unable to respond to requests in a timely manner. The `/health` endpoint must report `degraded` status when lag exceeds a defined threshold, enabling the load balancer to shed traffic before the process becomes unresponsive.

```typescript
import { monitorEventLoopDelay } from 'perf_hooks';

// Sample event loop delay at 20ms resolution
const histogram = monitorEventLoopDelay({ resolution: 20 });
histogram.enable();

// Event loop lag threshold: 100ms p99 is a signal of significant blocking
const EVENT_LOOP_LAG_THRESHOLD_MS = 100;

app.get('/health', (_req, res) => {
  const lagMs = histogram.percentile(99) / 1e6; // Convert nanoseconds to ms

  if (lagMs > EVENT_LOOP_LAG_THRESHOLD_MS) {
    res.status(200).json({
      status: 'degraded',
      checks: {
        eventLoop: {
          status: 'degraded',
          lagP99Ms: Math.round(lagMs),
          threshold: EVENT_LOOP_LAG_THRESHOLD_MS,
        },
      },
    });
    return;
  }

  res.status(200).json({
    status: 'healthy',
    checks: {
      eventLoop: { status: 'healthy', lagP99Ms: Math.round(lagMs) },
    },
  });
});
```
